+"""Evaluate CloudGuard findings against explicitly labelled ground truth.
+
+Ground-truth CSV schema:
+    resource_type,resource_id,rule_id,expected
+
+Finding CSVs must contain the same resource_type/resource_id pair. Matching
+is exact and case-sensitive; display names and partial identifiers are never
+used as substitutes for resource identity.
 
 Usage:
-    python evaluation/evaluate.py evaluation/ground_truth.csv cloudguard_scan_5.csv
-
-ground_truth.csv has one row per (resource, rule) you deliberately set up:
-    resource,rule_id,expected
-    cg-test-public-policy,S3-01,FAIL      <- you made this bucket public on purpose
-    cg-test-private,S3-01,PASS            <- this bucket is private, the tool must NOT flag it
-
-The findings CSV needs at least the columns rule_id and resource.
-A finding counts as a match when its rule_id is the same and the ground-truth
-resource name appears inside the finding's resource text (so "sg-0abc" matches
-"sg-0abc (cg-open-ssh)").
+    python evaluation/evaluate.py evaluation/ground_truth_template.csv findings.csv
 """
